PTX LB-self+alias+weak-load+acquire
"One thread, y and z aliases of global x. The weak load of y reads 2 from the later release store to z. The acquire load of y after it would make the pair an acquire pattern only if the first load were strong (8.8), so nothing synchronizes; with no alias fence nothing orders the load before the store to the alias (8.6). The release stores to y and z end in coherence order against program order (x == 1), which nothing forbids between aliases either: allowed."
{
x=0;
y @ generic aliases x;
z @ generic aliases x;
P0:r0=0;
P0:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,gpu 0              ;
 ld.weak r0, y               ;
 st.release.gpu y, 1         ;
 ld.acquire.gpu r1, y        ;
 st.release.gpu z, 2         ;
exists
(P0:r0 == 2 /\ P0:r1 == 1 /\ x == 1)
